  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Zot",
   "phonetic": "zot",
   "context": "Fool. People from Bruges are called Brugse zotten. Legend says they asked Maximilian of Habsburg to pay for a new madhouse, and he told them to just close the city gates.",
   "deepCutOrder": 2,
   "id": "bruges-deep-cut-2"
  },
  {
   "slot": "deep-cut",
   "local": "Schild en vriend",
   "phonetic": "SKHILT en VREENT",
   "context": "“Shield and friend.” In 1302, rebels in Bruges are said to have used it as a password, killing anyone who couldn’t pronounce it like a Fleming.",
   "deepCutOrder": 3,
